            <ArticleTitle>[Childhood asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>20-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Very frequently we have to deal with children who follow specific treatment to combat their repetitive episodes of breathing difficulty and wheezing. In many cases, they suffer from asthma. Hippocrates defined asthma as &quot;the condition which causes an excessive narrowing of the bronchi after a reaction with a provocative stimulus which usually does not produce any effect&quot;.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
